WEBVTT

00:00:04.713 --> 00:00:07.049
One, two! One, two, three!

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:40.624
There. I've finished fine-tuning
my "What If" machine.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:43.126
It can answer any "What if?" question

00:00:43.252 --> 00:00:46.255
accurate to within one-tenth
of a plausibility unit.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.549
That's so plausible I can't believe it.

00:00:48.674 --> 00:00:51.677
Who wants the machine to show
them an alternate reality?

00:00:51.802 --> 00:00:55.138
Ooh, ooh! I wanna know what
would happen if I were human.

00:00:55.264 --> 00:01:00.018
I mean, being a robot's great,
but we don't have emotions,

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:03.480
and sometimes that makes me very sad.

00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:06.775
Oh, lordy loo,
there he goes again.

00:01:06.859 --> 00:01:10.571
Well, let's give baby
what he wants.

00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:13.323
What if Bender were human?

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:21.582
Good news, everyone!
I've invented a way

00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:23.584
to turn Bender into a human

00:01:23.709 --> 00:01:27.296
using a process I call
reverse fossilization.

00:01:27.421 --> 00:01:30.799
- How does it work?
- Well, in regular fossilization,

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.010
flesh and bone turn to minerals.

00:01:33.135 --> 00:01:37.097
Realizing that, it was a simple matter
to reverse the process.

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:40.767
I've already tested it
by turning the toaster into a raccoon.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.191
Mmm. Kind of gamy.

00:01:47.316 --> 00:01:48.442
Are you ready, Bender?

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:51.361
I don't know. I'm beginning
to have some second thoughts.

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:08.795
Cover your shame, mon!

00:02:12.341 --> 00:02:16.595
It worked! Eat it everyone
who's never won a Nobel Prize!

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.264
And that includes you, Amy.

00:02:19.389 --> 00:02:22.768
So this is a human body, huh? Neat.

00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:26.063
Hey, my antenna's gone!

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:29.816
No, it just moved. I'm not getting
good reception on it, though.

00:02:30.192 --> 00:02:32.152
Maybe if I wiggle it around a little.

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:34.404
Bender, no.
You'll make God cry.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.367
Well, let's see what kind
of things this body can do.

00:02:38.492 --> 00:02:40.911
Hey, that's pretty fun.

00:02:42.287 --> 00:02:45.123
Being human is great!

00:02:48.043 --> 00:02:51.088
Hooray! It's just like Mardi Gras.

00:02:53.674 --> 00:02:56.593
Guys, guys, you gotta come
into the bathroom and look at this!

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:58.387
You're not gonna believe it.

00:02:58.512 --> 00:03:01.807
Bender, it's okay to be proud,
but don't be a showoff.

00:03:01.932 --> 00:03:03.600
Ooh.

00:03:03.684 --> 00:03:07.104
Whoa. You look a lot
better than you used to for some reason.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.523
You're not so bad yourself, big boy.

00:03:11.275 --> 00:03:13.652
Hey, that felt great!

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:19.032
- Nah, it's not working anymore.
- Speak for yourself.

00:03:25.747 --> 00:03:27.749
Whoa. This is awesome.

00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:30.419
Bender, you drank and smoked
when you were a robot.

00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:33.338
But now it's bad for me. Whoo!

00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:35.507
Speaking of which, try these nachos.

00:03:40.846 --> 00:03:45.809
Mmm. Why didn't anyone tell me
tasting things tasted so good?

00:03:50.272 --> 00:03:54.401
What's going on? That rhythm,
it's doing something to my human butt.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.913
Bender, part of being human
is having self-control.

00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:10.459
Oh, my God! I bet I can eat nachos and go
to the bathroom at the same time.

00:04:10.542 --> 00:04:12.377
No, Bender!

00:04:12.461 --> 00:04:14.171
- Let me go!
- No!

00:04:14.296 --> 00:04:17.132
Come, Bender.
It's time to go home and rest.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.051
I need you in top shape next week

00:04:19.176 --> 00:04:22.387
when I present you to
the Nobel Prize Committee.

00:04:22.513 --> 00:04:24.389
Bender?

00:04:24.515 --> 00:04:27.351
Good-bye, moderation!

00:04:27.476 --> 00:04:29.978
Come on shake your body
Baby, do the conga

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.147
I know you can't control
Yourself any longer

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:34.233
Feel the rhythm of the music
Getting stronger

00:04:34.358 --> 00:04:37.027
Don't you fight it till you tried it
Do the conga

00:04:55.379 --> 00:04:59.007
Is Bender still missing for a week?
Where is he already?

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:04.137
As I've said before,
I used reverse fossilization,

00:05:04.263 --> 00:05:08.725
which is the reverse
of regular, uh, eh...

00:05:08.851 --> 00:05:10.561
- Psst! We found him!
- Ah!

00:05:10.686 --> 00:05:15.399
Then without further stalling for time
I present to the Nobel judges,

00:05:15.524 --> 00:05:19.236
the first robot ever
turned into a human!

00:05:27.452 --> 00:05:30.289
My God!
He needs medical attention!

00:05:32.207 --> 00:05:35.002
300. failing.

00:05:35.085 --> 00:05:37.337
40?

00:05:37.588 --> 00:05:41.008
Well, that's not so bad.
No, I mean 40 pounds!

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:45.846
Eww. This, uh,
scientific breakthrough,

00:05:45.929 --> 00:05:50.142
uh, heralds a new dawn
in human/robot relations, yes.

00:05:51.059 --> 00:05:53.896
Come here and
give old Bender a kiss.

00:05:57.608 --> 00:06:00.485
Hey, you like grilled cheese?

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:07.034
And, uh, that's why I believe
I deserve the Nobel Prize.

00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:10.287
Not only do you not deserve
a Nobel Prize

00:06:10.412 --> 00:06:13.582
for loosing this bloated
man-ball upon the world,

00:06:13.707 --> 00:06:17.336
but you are hereby kicked out
of the Academy of Science!

00:06:19.922 --> 00:06:23.175
Wait! As men of science,

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:26.553
are not your minds
open to new ideas?

00:06:26.678 --> 00:06:29.681
I say, do not judge me

00:06:29.806 --> 00:06:33.644
until you have tried my way
of life for yourselves.

00:06:37.689 --> 00:06:41.818
Young man, you have opened our minds
and swayed our hearts.

00:06:41.944 --> 00:06:45.531
- Let us therefore...
- Party!

00:06:49.201 --> 00:06:51.370
Let's trash this place!

00:06:51.495 --> 00:06:53.830
Party!

00:06:53.956 --> 00:06:55.582
Whee!

00:06:57.125 --> 00:06:59.753
Come on shake your body
Baby, do the conga

00:06:59.878 --> 00:07:01.964
I know you can't control
Yourself any longer

00:07:02.047 --> 00:07:04.299
Feel the rhythm of the music
Getting stronger

00:07:05.676 --> 00:07:07.928
Bender, you were right.

00:07:08.053 --> 00:07:11.557
Truly you have lived more in
your one week of being human

00:07:11.682 --> 00:07:14.601
than the rest of us have
in our entire lives.

00:07:14.685 --> 00:07:16.353
Whoo!

00:07:16.478 --> 00:07:19.773
And so to recognize
your achievements,

00:07:19.898 --> 00:07:24.528
I hereby award you the Nobel Prize in

00:07:24.653 --> 00:07:27.114
uh, chemistry.

00:07:28.615 --> 00:07:30.576
Care to say a few words, Bender?

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:35.914
He's dead.

00:07:36.039 --> 00:07:38.542
- When did he die?
- Hmm.

00:07:38.625 --> 00:07:41.378
About twelve hours ago
when the party started.

00:07:41.545 --> 00:07:43.297
But he just said "Whoo!"

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.967
No, that was air escaping
from the folds of his fat.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.385
Whoo!

00:07:51.763 --> 00:07:53.807
Good night, sweet prince.

00:07:53.932 --> 00:07:57.978
You were the greatest man
any of us will ever know.

00:07:58.103 --> 00:08:02.316
Well, let's get him out of here.
He's starting to smell up the joint.

00:08:03.942 --> 00:08:05.485
Whoo!

00:08:05.611 --> 00:08:07.487
Whoo!

00:08:08.572 --> 00:08:10.073
Whoo!

00:08:10.199 --> 00:08:13.744
You watched it.
You can't un-watch it.

00:08:13.869 --> 00:08:15.579
Stay tuned for more...

00:08:23.337 --> 00:08:26.256
Who else has a question
for the "What If" machine?

00:08:26.465 --> 00:08:29.510
Scruffy? Katrina? Xanthor?

00:08:29.593 --> 00:08:33.764
Oh! I have one! I'm good at video games
and bad at everything else.

00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:36.600
That's why I wish life
were more like a video game.

00:08:36.725 --> 00:08:38.894
Can you put that in the form
of a question?

00:08:38.977 --> 00:08:42.105
Uh, what if
that thing I said?

00:08:44.274 --> 00:08:47.861
Oh, great machine,
we beseech thee,

00:08:47.945 --> 00:08:51.532
what if life were more
like a video game?

00:09:02.918 --> 00:09:04.753
Good evening, ignorant pigs.

00:09:04.878 --> 00:09:07.256
Put down your crack pipes
and your beer bongs

00:09:07.339 --> 00:09:10.509
and pay attention as I sign
an historic peace accord

00:09:10.592 --> 00:09:14.179
with Ambassador Kong
of Planet Nintendu 64.

00:09:14.263 --> 00:09:16.515
Wait a second.

00:09:16.598 --> 00:09:18.475
I know that monkey!
His name is Donkey.

00:09:18.559 --> 00:09:21.728
Monkeys aren't donkeys.
Quit messing with my head!

00:09:22.312 --> 00:09:25.649
I'll just put the old
John Q. Nixon on it.

00:09:28.694 --> 00:09:32.239
There. No major crap-ups.
You're on, Mr. Ambassador.

00:09:34.867 --> 00:09:36.618
What the...

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.298
Mama Mia!

00:09:49.381 --> 00:09:52.176
The cruel meatball of war
has-a rolled onto our laps,

00:09:52.593 --> 00:09:55.095
and-a ruined our
white-a pants of peace.

00:10:01.268 --> 00:10:04.897
Mr. Fry, rumor has it that you know the
secrets of the video game "Chance."

00:10:05.022 --> 00:10:06.899
Please, step into the war room.

00:10:11.403 --> 00:10:13.280
You'll be meeting
with General Colin Pacman.

00:10:13.363 --> 00:10:14.865
Wock-a, wock-a, wock-a!

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:16.366
Let's get down to business!

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:18.285
What can you tell us
about the Nintendians?

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.163
Well, sir, I spent all
of ninth grade studying them,

00:10:21.288 --> 00:10:24.541
except for that day when my eyeballs
started to bleed, and in my opinion...

00:10:26.877 --> 00:10:29.254
Quickly! To the escape tunnels.

00:10:29.379 --> 00:10:33.717
Wock-a, wock-a, wock-a, wock-a!

00:10:33.842 --> 00:10:36.720
Wock-a, wock-a, wock-a, wock-a!

00:10:36.845 --> 00:10:38.680
This way, damn it!

00:10:38.805 --> 00:10:40.682
Wock-a, wock-a, wock-a, wock-a!

00:10:40.807 --> 00:10:43.310
Wock-a, wock-a, wock-a, wock-a!
Mmm, delicious!

00:10:43.435 --> 00:10:45.604
Just like stale marshmallows!

00:10:45.687 --> 00:10:47.731
Ooh, and a cherry!

00:10:49.566 --> 00:10:52.653
Wock-a, wock-a, wock-a, wock-a!

00:10:52.778 --> 00:10:54.863
Hey, watch out!

00:10:56.823 --> 00:10:59.535
- Uh-oh!
- Oh, my God! He ate Fry!

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:01.912
Fry is dead!

00:11:02.037 --> 00:11:05.499
It's okay. I had another guy.

00:11:07.501 --> 00:11:09.795
Wock-a, wock-a...

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:24.184
Invaders, possibly from space!

00:11:24.351 --> 00:11:26.937
People of Earth,

00:11:27.104 --> 00:11:30.983
I am Lrrr of
the Planet Nintendu 64.

00:11:31.108 --> 00:11:34.903
Tremble in fear at our three
different kinds of ships.

00:11:35.028 --> 00:11:37.698
All right. It's Saturday night.

00:11:37.823 --> 00:11:43.120
I have no date, a two-liter bottle of
Shasta and my all-Rush mix tape.

00:11:43.245 --> 00:11:44.663
Let's rock!

00:11:44.788 --> 00:11:47.124
Today's Tom Sawyer
He gets high on you

00:11:47.249 --> 00:11:49.960
And the space he invades
He gets by on you

00:11:56.341 --> 00:11:59.261
We're losing ships, sir.
What are your orders?

00:11:59.386 --> 00:12:02.347
Increase speed, drop down
and reverse direction!

00:12:07.644 --> 00:12:09.897
I've still got a trick
or two up my sleeve.

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:12.441
Watch as I fire upwards
through our own shield!

00:12:12.524 --> 00:12:15.027
He's a madman!

00:12:15.402 --> 00:12:17.404
A madman!

00:12:24.828 --> 00:12:27.080
It's working. Victory is assured.

00:12:27.206 --> 00:12:30.417
My retirement tomorrow
will be all the sweeter.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:34.046
I'm hit!

00:12:34.171 --> 00:12:36.465
So cold.

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.927
No!

00:12:40.052 --> 00:12:42.387
Amy, tend to the Widow Pacman.

00:12:42.513 --> 00:12:46.058
Wock-a, wock-a, wock-a.

00:12:47.893 --> 00:12:49.686
Drop down and increase speed!

00:12:51.897 --> 00:12:53.690
One ship is left only.

00:12:55.067 --> 00:12:56.944
Come on, Fry! Get it!

00:12:57.069 --> 00:13:00.113
It's moving too fast!
Oh, I could never get the last one.

00:13:00.239 --> 00:13:03.700
My brother always got it for me.

00:13:07.663 --> 00:13:11.208
Drop down! Reverse direction!
Prepare for landing.

00:13:25.055 --> 00:13:28.433
You are defeated!
Instead of shooting where I was,

00:13:28.559 --> 00:13:31.770
you should have shot at where
I was going to be.

00:13:36.483 --> 00:13:39.236
All your base are belong to us.

00:13:41.029 --> 00:13:44.867
What do you monsters want?

00:13:44.992 --> 00:13:47.870
One thing, and one thing only.

00:13:47.995 --> 00:13:51.748
Quarters! A million allowances
worth of quarters!

00:13:51.874 --> 00:13:53.917
No slugs or tokens!

00:13:54.042 --> 00:13:57.880
- Fork 'em over! Fork 'em over!
- Forget it, you pixilated pirates!

00:13:58.005 --> 00:14:01.842
We need those quarters to do our laundry!

00:14:01.967 --> 00:14:05.470
But... But space invaders
need to do laundry too.

00:14:05.596 --> 00:14:07.472
I mean, look at Donkey Kong here.

00:14:07.598 --> 00:14:09.850
Have you smelled
his loincloth lately?

00:14:09.975 --> 00:14:11.852
- Yes.
- Go away!

00:14:11.977 --> 00:14:14.688
We're not giving you
our quarters no matter what!

00:14:14.813 --> 00:14:18.275
Well, then what if we throw
our laundry in with yours?

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.402
- Would that be acceptable?
- I guess so.

00:14:20.527 --> 00:14:22.571
Okay then, that settles that.

00:14:22.654 --> 00:14:26.533
But if this cape shrinks,
consider your species extinct!

00:14:26.658 --> 00:14:28.785
Bravo!

00:14:28.911 --> 00:14:30.621
That'll be hard to top!

00:14:30.704 --> 00:14:32.748
I pity the next...

00:14:32.831 --> 00:14:35.250
Tales of Interest.

00:14:42.299 --> 00:14:45.511
Well, there's time
for one last question.

00:14:45.636 --> 00:14:48.847
Let's turn to the "Who Asked"
machine to see who's next?

00:14:50.599 --> 00:14:54.019
Um, uh, Amy.

00:14:54.144 --> 00:14:55.812
I mean Leela.

00:14:55.938 --> 00:14:57.606
Okay.

00:14:57.689 --> 00:15:00.984
As an alien who was abandoned on Earth,

00:15:01.068 --> 00:15:03.320
I've never really
belonged anywhere.

00:15:03.403 --> 00:15:04.905
Boo hoo!

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:07.908
Ow!

00:15:08.325 --> 00:15:09.952
So my question is this...

00:15:10.035 --> 00:15:12.829
What if I found my true home?

00:15:14.164 --> 00:15:16.291
Ow!

00:15:24.299 --> 00:15:26.844
Where are we?

00:15:42.276 --> 00:15:45.696
Nibbler, I don't think
we're in New New York anymore.

00:15:48.574 --> 00:15:54.079
Geez, apparently the phrase "tone it
down" doesn't exist on this planet.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:57.040
Oh, no!

00:15:57.165 --> 00:15:59.835
We hit someone!
Quick, back into the ship!

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.629
Ooh, nice boots.

00:16:02.754 --> 00:16:04.298
Yuck!

00:16:04.381 --> 00:16:07.467
Look, everyone!
She killed the Manwitch of the West!

00:16:07.593 --> 00:16:10.262
A witch?

00:16:10.387 --> 00:16:13.682
That explains how these boots
magically appeared on my feet.

00:16:13.807 --> 00:16:16.518
No, you stole them.
We saw you!

00:16:16.643 --> 00:16:20.105
Well, it's hard to find
shoes that fit me.

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:22.107
So anyway,
who are you people?

00:16:22.232 --> 00:16:24.818
Haven't I seen you
in some copyrighted movie?

00:16:24.943 --> 00:16:27.237
We resemble
But are legally distinct

00:16:27.362 --> 00:16:29.698
From the Lollipop Guild
The Lollipop

00:16:39.291 --> 00:16:42.419
Greetings, Leela.
I'm the Cute Witch of the North.

00:16:42.544 --> 00:16:45.214
Yeah. Can anyone fix my ship
so I can get home?

00:16:45.339 --> 00:16:48.342
Abraca-duh.
Just ask the professor.

00:16:48.467 --> 00:16:51.970
He lives in the Emerald Laboratory down
Martin Luther King Boulevard.

00:16:52.095 --> 00:16:56.016
You mean that Yellow Brick Road?
The City Council renamed it in 1975.

00:16:56.141 --> 00:16:59.061
Ooh, those are great shoes!

00:16:59.186 --> 00:17:02.105
- Oh, thank you.
- Do they come in women's sizes?

00:17:10.405 --> 00:17:14.034
Okay, crow.
Prepare to be scared.

00:17:14.451 --> 00:17:18.872
"And then... honk, honk...
The car honked its own horn!"

00:17:18.997 --> 00:17:21.458
Wow. A talking scarecrow.

00:17:21.583 --> 00:17:25.254
Wanna come with us to see the professor?
He might be able to give you a brain.

00:17:25.379 --> 00:17:28.090
Hey! That's not
a nice thing to say.

00:17:28.215 --> 00:17:31.218
Beer! Beer!

00:17:31.343 --> 00:17:33.095
Whiskey okay?

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:40.102
Now, did you say you're off
to see the professor?

00:17:40.227 --> 00:17:42.479
'Cause I could use a heart...
a human heart.

00:17:42.604 --> 00:17:44.982
I need to pump a lot of blood
out of my basement.

00:17:46.024 --> 00:17:48.360
And I'm the other guy, Courage.

00:17:48.443 --> 00:17:50.821
Not enough of it.
Need some from what's-his-name.

00:17:55.617 --> 00:17:57.578
Damn this D.S.L.!

00:18:01.498 --> 00:18:03.333
Fly, my stupids!

00:18:03.458 --> 00:18:05.335
Fly out and get them!

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:08.922
But, Mommy, you promised
you'd bake monkey cake today.

00:18:09.047 --> 00:18:11.508
By "monkey cake,"
I meant your ass!

00:18:17.222 --> 00:18:19.224
Man, we've been skipping for hours.

00:18:19.349 --> 00:18:21.185
I need to pull over and take "The Wiz."

00:18:23.854 --> 00:18:26.398
What, do I smell or something?

00:18:30.944 --> 00:18:34.156
- Why did you bring us here?
- And why did I have to take a cab?

00:18:34.281 --> 00:18:38.410
I'll tell you why I brought you here,
you twice-baked barf bags!

00:18:38.493 --> 00:18:41.747
Because I've always wanted
a daughter to love.

00:18:41.872 --> 00:18:44.166
You wanna get adopted,
you little skank?

00:18:44.291 --> 00:18:47.336
And live here
and be a witch like you?

00:18:47.461 --> 00:18:49.254
Yeah, all right.

00:18:49.379 --> 00:18:52.799
As long as I get to hurt people
and not just dance around at the equinox.

00:18:52.883 --> 00:18:57.304
- Absolutely.
- Oh, Mommy! I found my true home!

00:18:57.387 --> 00:18:59.056
That's great, Leela!

00:18:59.515 --> 00:19:03.352
I've heard worse excuses
to drink. Oops!

00:19:03.435 --> 00:19:06.104
I'm melting! Oh!

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:11.527
Who would have thought a small amount
of liquid would ever fall on me?

00:19:13.487 --> 00:19:16.490
Well, no point in
lettin' her go to waste.

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:28.460
- Yes?
- We're here to see the professor.

00:19:28.585 --> 00:19:30.712
No one sees the mighty professor!

00:19:30.838 --> 00:19:33.423
Who's there, Hermes?
Is it visitors?

00:19:33.507 --> 00:19:35.717
- I want to see them!
- It's nobody!

00:19:35.801 --> 00:19:38.595
Now sign that will I gave you!
He's not here.

00:19:38.971 --> 00:19:41.390
Oh, for the love of Benji.

00:19:47.729 --> 00:19:49.690
I am the professor!

00:19:49.773 --> 00:19:52.985
Great and, uh, forgetful!

00:19:57.197 --> 00:19:59.783
Now, what do you nice kids want?

00:19:59.992 --> 00:20:01.869
Nothing! I'm leaving!

00:20:01.952 --> 00:20:05.372
But if you have extra courage,
I'd haul it away for you maybe?

00:20:05.497 --> 00:20:08.500
Oh, blithery poop,
my cowardly lobster!

00:20:08.625 --> 00:20:10.210
You don't need courage.

00:20:10.335 --> 00:20:15.507
After all, who needs courage
when you have a gun?

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:20.888
Now, world. You put your hands up!

00:20:21.013 --> 00:20:24.099
And you, lad, all you need is a brain.

00:20:24.224 --> 00:20:25.976
Why does everyone keep saying that?

00:20:26.101 --> 00:20:28.312
This is a stickup!

00:20:28.437 --> 00:20:30.314
Give me the bag, old man!

00:20:30.439 --> 00:20:33.942
Here you go, my friend.

00:20:34.067 --> 00:20:37.321
Five thousand
Professor Land fun bucks.

00:20:37.446 --> 00:20:39.364
Oh, crap.

00:20:39.489 --> 00:20:42.284
As for you, young lady,

00:20:42.409 --> 00:20:44.369
you want to go home, right?

00:20:44.494 --> 00:20:48.332
No, not anymore. I want to stay here
and become the new wicked witch.

00:20:48.457 --> 00:20:53.128
Nonsense! Now click your big honking
boots together three times,

00:20:53.253 --> 00:20:55.547
and wish to go home to Kansas

00:20:55.672 --> 00:20:59.885
to live in poverty with your dirt-farming,
teetotaling aunt and uncle.

00:20:59.968 --> 00:21:02.804
Uh, all right.
Here I go.

00:21:06.517 --> 00:21:10.020
There's no place like...
I wanna be a witch!

00:21:19.321 --> 00:21:22.699
Oh, no! Help!
What's happening?

00:21:22.824 --> 00:21:26.995
Uh, sorry. I think there's a problem
with your upstairs toilet.

00:21:32.376 --> 00:21:35.045
Wake up!

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:37.840
Leela, are you all right?
You got wanged on the head.

00:21:37.965 --> 00:21:40.759
I was having
the most wonderful dream,

00:21:40.884 --> 00:21:44.221
except you were there,
and you were there, and you were there.

00:21:44.346 --> 00:21:46.431
Never mind, Professor.
She came to.

00:21:46.576 --> 00:21:49.078
Oh, so close.

00:21:49.142 --> 00:21:51.144
There's always next year, Professor.

00:21:51.228 --> 00:21:53.480
There's always next year.